<!--
    Outlined `objc_retain_x<N>` returns in x0, not x<N> (`option objc on`, `objcarc on|off`).

    Issue: clang's outlined retain takes the object in x19 and returns the retained
    object in x0, the way every call-site reads it: `bl objc_retain_x19; mov x20, x0`.
    The prototype declared the result in x19, so the copy into x20 took whatever x0
    held before the call. On the Toyota app `-[AddMileageViewController viewDidLoad]`
    therefore passed `vtable#7.method` the metatype from the type-metadata accessor
    (`vtable#7.method(v2)`) where the call's `self` was meant.

    Fixture `macho_objc_outlined_retain_arm64` (source `.s` beside it, hand-written
    because clang does not outline ARC retains from source here): the entry keeps
    `self` in x19, calls an accessor that clobbers x0, builds the objc_super and
    calls `bl _objc_retain_x19`, then `mov x20, x0` and calls the callee with it.

    Pass 1 (default): the call's argument is the entry's `self` (`a0`), the retain is
    hidden. Pass 2 (`objcarc off`): the retain is shown with its argument and result,
    `objc_retain_x19(a0)`, and the call takes that result.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_objc_outlined_retain_arm64</com>
  <com>option objc on</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x1000004c4</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/macho_objc_outlined_retain_arm64</com>
  <com>option objc on</com>
  <com>option objcarc off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load addr 0x1000004c4</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDRET #1: default passes the entry's self to the callee, not the accessor's metadata" min="1" max="1">_holder_vtable7\(a0\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDRET #2: default never passes the accessor's result to the callee" min="0" max="0">_holder_vtable7\(\(void \*\)_holder_type_accessor\(\)\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDRET #3: the entry takes its self as the parameter the call forwards" min="2" max="2">_holder_viewDidLoad\([^)]*a0\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="OUTLINEDRET #4: off shows the retain with its argument and the result the call takes" min="1" max="1">_holder_vtable7\(objc_retain_x19\(a0\)\);</stringmatch>
